                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14791456-1d0c-383e-9785-e00719994804",
                        "entry_id": "82e3df6e-f9c0-3444-b47b-d5655fc4de46",
                        "glosses": [
                            "physikalische Größe, das (Kreuz-)Produkt von Kraft und Kraftarm bei Rotationen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "physics"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5be33d07-42ca-44df-8eee-6344813927fb",
                                "sense_id": "14791456-1d0c-383e-9785-e00719994804",
                                "text": "Der bei Automobilen verwendete Begriff ‚maximales Drehmoment eines Verbrennungsmotors bei einer bestimmten Drehzahl‘ bezeichnet das maximale vom Motor an der Kurbelwelle abgegebene Drehmoment."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "55103cff-8fb7-4a12-be3f-2a2deeb274dc",
                        "source_entry_id": "82e3df6e-f9c0-3444-b47b-d5655fc4de46",
                        "source_sense_id": "14791456-1d0c-383e-9785-e00719994804",
                        "source_sense_description": "Physik, Mechanik: physikalische Größe, das (Kreuz-)Produkt von Kraft und Kraftarm bei Rotationen",
                        "target_lang_word": "angular momentum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "angular momentum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47126f51-2d59-34ca-bc11-63abcd9b5f93",
                                        "entry_id": "1b9a534a-c7b6-3c70-a517-2933925d1a00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The vector product that describes the rotary inertia of a system about an axis and is conserved in a closed system. For an isolated rigid body, it is a measure of the extent to which an object will continue to rotate in the absence of an applied torque."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "effa61c0-2897-4d9e-8813-2c76d1343e06",
                        "source_entry_id": "82e3df6e-f9c0-3444-b47b-d5655fc4de46",
                        "source_sense_id": "14791456-1d0c-383e-9785-e00719994804",
                        "source_sense_description": "Physik, Mechanik: physikalische Größe, das (Kreuz-)Produkt von Kraft und Kraftarm bei Rotationen",
                        "target_lang_word": "torque",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "torque",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8328beb-a8be-3c31-8d35-9bc8db53a110",
                                        "entry_id": "5583d6fe-d6e1-33de-b47b-d4c16ed613cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rotational or twisting effect of a force; a moment of force, defined for measurement purposes as an equivalent straight line force multiplied by the distance from the axis of rotation (SI unit newton-metre or N·m; imperial unit pound-foot or lb·ft, not to be confused with the foot pound-force, commonly \\\"foot-pound\\\", a unit of work or energy)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bcc5500-2473-4629-b665-9277e2c22710",
                                                "sense_id": "c8328beb-a8be-3c31-8d35-9bc8db53a110",
                                                "text": "The relative strengths of the various torques will depend on both the spacecraft environment and the form and structure of the spacecraft itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c329321a-9d84-4fb8-93e1-597bca88a071",
                                                "sense_id": "c8328beb-a8be-3c31-8d35-9bc8db53a110",
                                                "text": "The drillhead produces the drilling rotation and torque but also must slide out of position to allow the machine to manipulate the finisher drill steel and consumables."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "torque",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecb1f362-decb-314a-b6f2-e4d31ac8770a",
                                        "entry_id": "ae78a405-40c6-3b44-9ba8-68adb3423d12",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make something rotate about an axis by imparting torque to it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "torque",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8d8d48f-615b-393a-9f23-de0c191301c5",
                                        "entry_id": "5feb37e2-fab3-385a-a65d-25054393177d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tightly braided necklace or collar, often made of metal, worn by various early European peoples."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57d8018c-4556-4de7-9aae-341cc8899356",
                                                "sense_id": "d8d8d48f-615b-393a-9f23-de0c191301c5",
                                                "text": "But there are the lesser sub-kings of Wales, true to the immemorial schisms amongst themselves, which destroyed the realm of Ambrosius, and rendered vain the arm of Arthur. With their torques of gold, and wild eyes, and hair cut round ears and brow, they stare on the scene."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68db49f1-8728-40f7-8fbb-4f795e2a93b8",
                                                "sense_id": "d8d8d48f-615b-393a-9f23-de0c191301c5",
                                                "text": "People of high rank also wore a torque of gold round the neck, and I observed that our guide had one on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b13a773-87fd-4775-a712-e1b898705413",
                                                "sense_id": "d8d8d48f-615b-393a-9f23-de0c191301c5",
                                                "text": "“When I see mother next it will be to put a golden torque round her neck,” said the young giant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d571c29-d1b2-4143-b3e2-8cc5b0020f0b",
                                                "sense_id": "d8d8d48f-615b-393a-9f23-de0c191301c5",
                                                "text": "Nor did he reneg, but doled out rings\nand torques at the table."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99bcbd0a-5cca-42e3-918d-553cec75b0d0",
                        "source_entry_id": "82e3df6e-f9c0-3444-b47b-d5655fc4de46",
                        "source_sense_id": "14791456-1d0c-383e-9785-e00719994804",
